{
  "description": "Widget-block parity between the backend parser (App\\Domain\\AI\\Entities\\Conversations\\Widgets\\WidgetBlocks) and the frontend rendering pipeline (normalizeServerMessageToMarkdown -> remark + remarkGfm + remark-directive + remarkWidgetFencePlugin + conversationWidgetAstPlugin). Each case: the markdown, the blocks the backend reads (syntax, outcome, isClosed, the type as written, the origin the block's emittedBy names -- null for a block without the field, i.e. the model) and frontendRenderedWidgetNames. frontendRenderedWidgetNames means ONLY 'widget nodes mounted by registry name' (the canonical hName conversationWidgetAstPlugin resolves) -- it is NOT a claim about what the customer visibly sees: ConversationWidgetHost's feature gate can swap in an upsell, its error boundary can swallow a throwing widget, and WindowedWidget can replace an off-screen widget with a placeholder. Two paths are deliberately not represented by this column: the STREAMING bubble (ConversationMessageWidgets.tsx only strips the {preCallMessage} sentinel while a message is still arriving, with no repair and no naked-JSON referencing) and widgetNamesInMarkdown (markdown-contains-widget.ts, a separate regex-based scan the message list uses to detect a superseded widget, which never runs this remark pipeline). A case where the two legitimately disagree carries a 'divergence' text: it is LISTED, never claimed to agree. The cases name the package's own widgets (QuickReplies, MultiChoice, ToolTrace), so they render under the package's registry alone; an application keeps its own cases with its own widgets in a fixture of its own. The backend side is asserted by WidgetBlocksParityTest (PHPUnit), the frontend side by _widget-block-parity.spec.ts (vitest).",
